      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The effect of bicycle ergometry on lipid peroxidation was examined in 43 coronary patients. An increase in malonic dialdehyde, a secondary product of lipid peroxidation, was detected in patients with post-infarction cardiosclerosis, an evidence of intensified lipid peroxidation in systemic tissues. It is proposed that natural antioxidants be used to prevent myocardial metabolic disorders in coronary patients."},
